<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet>
  <title>26: The Fourier transform</title>

  <exercise workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>Explain why
  <md>
  \fourier[xf(x)] = -i\frac{d}{d\omega}\fourier[f].
  </md>
  It may be easiest to start with the right hand side.</p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>Explain why the Shift Theorem is true:
  <md>
  \fourier[f(x-\beta)] = e^{i\omega\beta}\fourier[f].
  </md>
  Suggestion: try a change of variable <m>y=x-\beta</m>.</p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
